      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here's a quick checklist for you:\n\n1. **Different Requirements for Transit and Entry Visas**: Transit visas are for stops during transit and must have heads and shoulders clear of the documents, while entry visas must remain in the passport.\n2. **Country-Specific Needs**: Singapore, Vietnam, and Thailand have specific procedures and requirements for transit visas or visas recorded in a machine-readable card. Double-check the latest requirements for each country.\n3. **Single vs. Multiple Entry Visa**: Ensure your destination visa covers the total duration of stay. Singapore, Vietnam, and Thailand might have different entry visa requirements than transit visas.\n4. **Business and Leisure Travel**: Whether the engineers are traveling for personal or business reasons can change visa requirements, as some countries treat tourist and business travellers differently.\n5. **Visa-on-Arrival Exemptions**: Some countries permit visa-on-arrival for skilled workers travelling for specific reasons, such as engineering projects or international conferences. Check if these apply to your group.\n6. **Advance Lookups and Alerts**: Use government travel websites or consular services to check up-to-date visa rules and conditions before departure. A layover visa extension may be available.\n\nBy following these points, your",
